[
  [preserved,summary];
  [ACTORBIT,"Animate creature (NPC, or the player's avatar); gates fight/give/talk/wake/throw-at and \"the X is holding:\" listing, and counts as a live being in room-occupancy checks (INFESTED?)."],
  [BURNBIT,"Object is flammable: BURN consumes it, CUT-with-weapon shreds it, and LIGHT/turn-on redirects to burning it (paper, wood, boats, leaves)."],
  [CLIMBBIT,"Object is climbable; the noun for CLIMB/WALK UP|DOWN resolves to it (trees, stairs, ladders, cliffs, chimney) - matched purely via grammar, never tested in code."],
  [CONTBIT,"Object is a container that can hold other objects (chests, boxes, doors-as-passages, even creatures that carry loot); gates OPEN/CLOSE/LOOK-INSIDE/FILL."],
  [DOORBIT,"Object is a door/openable portal; gates OPEN/CLOSE/KNOCK/look-inside and WALK-THROUGH, whose passage is gated on its OPENBIT."],
  [DRINKBIT,"Object is a drinkable liquid (water); handled by DRINK/EAT."],
  [FIGHTBIT,"Runtime combat state: this creature is actively fighting the player - set when attacked, drives villain counter-attacks and exit-blocking, cleared when combat ends (carried on the GLOBAL-OBJECTS master as a default, but in play only toggled on villains)."],
  [FLAMEBIT,"Object can produce open flame; when also ONBIT it is a live flame (the FLAMING? test) used to light or burn things; cleared with ONBIT when extinguished (candles, torch, lit match)."],
  [FOODBIT,"Object is edible; handled by EAT."],
  [INVISIBLE,"Object is absent from play: excluded from parser scope (THIS-IT?) and from being touched (ACCESSIBLE?) and never auto-listed; toggled constantly to make things appear/vanish (the thief, post-puzzle scenery, pocketed treasure)."],
  [LIGHTBIT,"Object is a switchable lamp/light source; gates TURN ON/OFF, which toggles its ONBIT. Distinct from ONBIT, which is the lit state itself."],
  [MAZEBIT,"(Zork 1) Room is a maze cell; its TOUCHBIT is cleared after each look so it always re-prints in full, and the thief roams it specially."],
  [NDESCBIT,"\"No-describe\": suppress this object's automatic room/contents listing (scenery, walls, fixtures, or items already named in prose); cleared when first taken so it then lists normally."],
  [NONLANDBIT,"Room is not solid footing (air, water, chasm); changes fall/grue handling, makes dropped contents vanish, and requires a vehicle; some rooms toggle it (a reservoir when filled)."],
  [NWALLBIT,"(Zork 2) Room flag on the open volcano-shaft (VAIR) air rooms and one cage room; declared but never read by the shipped engine (vestigial / reserved)."],
  [ONBIT,"Lit/active state: a room that is inherently lit, or a lamp/candle/torch/machine currently switched on; the runtime light test (LIT?) keys off it and lit objects print \"(providing light)\"."],
  [OPENBIT,"Object is currently open; toggled by OPEN/CLOSE and required to see into, reach into, put into, eat-drink from, or walk through it."],
  [READBIT,"Object bears readable text; gates READ (cleared if the text is destroyed, e.g. a burned label)."],
  [RLANDBIT,"Room is dry land you can stand on; entering a non-land room needs a vehicle, and DISEMBARK requires it (a reservoir toggles it as it drains/fills). Set on nearly every room."],
  [RMUNGBIT,"Dual-purpose: on a ROOM, wrecked/impassable - GOTO refuses entry and prints its replacement description (GWIM also maps the bit to ROOMS for \"look\"-type grammar); on a LIGHT SOURCE, marks the lamp/candle as burned-out/used-up."],
  [SACREDBIT,"Object/room is off-limits to the thief: he will not steal a sacred object nor enter or stash loot in a sacred room (set on aboveground/temple rooms, key treasures, and the player avatar)."],
  [SEARCHBIT,"Container whose contents are in parser scope without being opened (the parser recurses into it during noun resolution)."],
  [STAGGERED,"Dual-purpose: in Zork 1 a runtime combat stun (a STAGGER blow sets it; the dazed combatant wastes its next turn, then it clears); in Zork 2 reused as a static tag marking wizard's-case treasures for the death/scatter routine (RANDOMIZE-OBJECTS)."],
  [SURFACEBIT,"Object is a surface things rest on top of (table, altar, pedestal, shelf); contents stay in scope and list as \"sitting on\", and PUT-ON / LOOK-ON resolve to it."],
  [TAKEBIT,"Object can be picked up and carried; required by TAKE and the take routine, and by take-all and the thief's stealing logic."],
  [TOOLBIT,"Object can serve as an implement; the grammar's \"with\" instrument slot for DIG/LOCK/UNLOCK/OPEN/TURN/TIE-UP/INFLATE resolves to it (shovel, wrench, keys, screwdriver, putty)."],
  [TOUCHBIT,"\"Encountered\" state: set the first time a room is entered or an object is opened/taken/put/handled; selects subsequent (LDESC) over first-time (FDESC) description and suppresses re-listing - frequently cleared to force a re-description."],
  [TRANSBIT,"Object is transparent: its contents are visible/in-scope and it can be read or seen through even while closed (bottle, flask, glass cases, crystal palantiri)."],
  [TRYTAKEBIT,"Manipulable-in-place: an implicit \"(Taken)\" before a verb is satisfied without actually moving the object, and it is excluded from take-all (fixed scenery, creatures, immovable features you can still act on)."],
  [TURNBIT,"Object can be turned/rotated; gates TURN (bolt, switch, dial, sundial, key, menhir)."],
  [VEHBIT,"Object is a rideable vehicle (boat, balloon, bucket, time machine); gates BOARD/DISEMBARK/LAUNCH, enables crossing non-land rooms, and drives the \"in the X\" room/inventory display."],
  [WEAPONBIT,"Object can be wielded as a weapon; required as the instrument of ATTACK/CUT/MUNG/SWING and factored into combat strength (sword, knife, axe, stiletto)."],
  [WEARBIT,"Object is wearable; TAKE auto-wears it, it shows \"(being worn)\", and worn items are exempt from the carry/fumble count and weigh only 1 (crown, ring, cloak, hood, amulet)."]
]